<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan money rates stay low on surplus funds.</title>
<headline>Pakistan money rates stay low on surplus funds.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's money rates stayed low on Saturday amid surplus liquidity and dealers said they would remained pegged at similar levels till the central bank conducts an open market market operation next week.</p>
<p>Overnight rates traded in the range of 2.0 to 3.0 percent, a dealer said. &quot;Most of the time lending pressure was seen and the market ended with surplus funds,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Amir Zia 9221-5685192</p>
